--TEST--
An `@see` whose target no class declares is `E0323`, resolved against the same member table a `Class::member` reference is — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`: `@see` names a member
// the compiler can find, so a name nothing declares is a diagnostic rather
// than a link that quietly goes nowhere.
/// Every entry this ledger has taken.
///
/// @see Ledger::missing
final class Ledger {
    public static function total(): int {
        return 0;
    }
}
echo Ledger::total(), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0323]: `Ledger` has no member named `missing` for `@see` to resolve
  --> %s:7:10
  |
7 | /// @see Ledger::missing
  |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no such member

